@page "/rules"

<PageTitle>Rules and Features — MistChess</PageTitle>

<div class="game-page rules-page">
    <section class="hero-row">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">QUICK GUIDE</p>
            <h1>Rules of the mist.</h1>
            <p class="hero-copy">The game follows standard chess rules, with one twist: each player has limited visibility.</p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <div class="rules-grid">
        <article class="rule-card"><span class="rule-index">01</span><h2>Fog of War</h2><p>You can see your pieces and the squares they attack. King Radar also reveals a five-by-five area around your king.</p></article>
        <article class="rule-card"><span class="rule-index">02</span><h2>Acoustic Footsteps</h2><p>When your opponent moves near one of your pieces, the destination square briefly ripples. The ripple shows movement without revealing the piece's type or color.</p></article>
        <article class="rule-card"><span class="rule-index">03</span><h2>How to win</h2><p>In Fog of War, capture the king to win. Classic Chess follows the engine's standard rules for check, checkmate, stalemate, and draws.</p></article>
        <article class="rule-card"><span class="rule-index">04</span><h2>Special moves</h2><p>Castling, en passant, and pawn promotion to a queen, rook, bishop, or knight are supported.</p></article>
    </div>
    <section class="about-block">
        <p class="eyebrow">HOW TO PLAY</p>
        <h2>Select a piece, then choose a square.</h2>
        <p>Against a bot, choose from five profiles, pick a side, and select a game variant. In online games, the server validates every move and sends each player a separate view of the board. Use Replay to review each move from different perspectives.</p>
        <a class="primary-button link-button" href="/">Start playing <span>↗</span></a>
    </section>
</div>
